{14 = 14-21}
61=14.	(@wDN{Nisaba} speaks:) @q[Nisaba,]{“In my house, may the moonlight in my house, the moonlight, 
65=15.	the glorious sky in my house, the moonlight, 
69=16.	the glorious night in my house -- may the glorious sky, 
73=17.	the glorious night in my house not leave me (?)! 
77=18.	The moonlight is obscured by the walls from my man, from my man. 
81=19.	The moonlight, the glorious sky, from my man, the moonlight, 
85=20.	the glorious night, from my man, the glorious sky, 
89=21.	the glorious night is obscured by the walls from my man.”} 

{22 = 22-30}
93=22.	@q{“In the moonlight, in the pure place of moonlight I lie down alone. 
97=23.	In the moonlight which fills the hills, the pure place, I lie down alone. 
101=24.	By the cedar mountains where @wDN{Enlil} lies, I lie down alone. …… I weep a bitter lament. 
105=25.	…… lying in the moonlight, I weep a bitter lament. 
109=26.	…… which sets aglow …… shines forth. I am distraught. 
113=27.	The moonlight which sets aglow the glorious sky shines forth. I am distraught. 
117=28.	The moonlight which sets aglow the glorious night shines forth. 
121=29.	I am distraught -- which sets aglow the glorious sky, the glorious night, shines forth. 
125=30.	I am distraught.”} 

{31 = 31-33}
129=31.	Even now that the pure place knows daylight, amid her awe-inspiring splendour, still she weeps. 
133=32.	Amid her awe-inspiring splendour, still Mother @wDN{Ezina-Kusu} weeps. Fate and fortune! 
137=33.	Amid her awe-inspiring splendour, still she weeps. 

